     I don't know where any actual patch is, but the file to
change is the top-level Makefile (or sys/unix/Makefile.top
if you haven't run setup.sh yet).  The line you care about is
  -rm -rf $(HACKDIR) $(VARDIR)
but it isn't actually necessary to disable that if you can
remember to use `make update' instead of `make install'.

     Some old newsgroup discussion recommends editing the
Makefile to change target name "install:" to "newinstall:"
(and maybe someone created a patch for that).  If you've
done that, trying to execute `make install' will fail, and
then you'll have to choose between `make update' (which
leaves the score file and any other old stuff intact) and
`make newinstall' (which will clear out everything from
nethack's directory before putting a full set of new files
there).


